WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.469 size:78% position:39%
-Welcome to the show!
-Thank you so much

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:04.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
for having me!
-I´m so happy to have you.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.872 size:84% position:42%
This book is fantastic.

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
It takes place
in Shaker Heights, Ohio,

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:09.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is where you´re from.
-Yes.

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:10.844
-It takes place in the ´90s.

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:14.114
Why -- I want to start with why
you chose to put it in the ´90s.

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:17.217
-The first reason was that
it gave me a really good excuse

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:19.019 size:88% position:44%
to relive my teen years,
which is not something

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I ever thought
I would actually say.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-But the real reason is that

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:25.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wanted to look at sort of,
how far we´d come

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then how far
we hadn´t come

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
from race, class,
all of those issues.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember living
in Shaker Heights in the ´90s,

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:36.036
and the way that we talked
about race was really to say,

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:37.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I don´t see race."

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:39.539 size:81% position:41%
And now that´s sort of
a punch line, right?

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:43.343
And so I wanted to look at the
ways that we haven´t really gone

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:44.644
as far as we think we have.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:47.547
-Also, just reading it, I
realized, oh, this is nice,

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, in the ´90s, like, the
fact that anyone has

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.818
a cellphone is mind-blowing.

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:55.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so teenagers communicate
the way it sounds like

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:57.157
you communicated as a teenager.
-Exactly.

00:00:57.157 --> 00:01:00.326
So, it was before cell phones,
before any kind of social media,

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:03.129 size:84% position:42%
before the Internet was
even really a thing.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.632
I needed the characters to have
a little bit of space

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:08.001
to have secrets, ´cause these
characters have a lot of things

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:10.937
they´re keeping from each other
and trying to hide

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
and leave behind parts
of their past.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it´s a lot harder
to do that now

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I wanted them
to have that space.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so you put it
in Shaker Heights,

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this is the town
you grew up in.

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:21.414 size:84% position:42%
But I´m wondering if in
the writing of the book

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.283
and the researching in the book,
did you find out new things

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
about where you were from?
-I did.

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:28.855
I learned way more about the
Shakers, the religious community

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:31.224
that used to own the land
that became Shaker Heights,

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:33.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
than any reasonable person
needs to know.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So anything you want to know
about the Shakers now,

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can talk about.
-Yeah, all the --

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you went to the library,
all the Shaker books

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
were available,
none were checked out?

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They were. The Shaker Heights
Public Library actually has

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
a really great
local history room,

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:48.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this is where local
history librarians do the job

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:49.776 size:78% position:39%
when nobody else can.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
She pointed me
to old newspapers,

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:52.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
all kinds of books

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the Shakers
and everything.

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:57.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I also learned that a lot
of things that I thought

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.886
were normal from growing up
in Shaker Heights were actually

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:03.323 size:75% position:38%
not normal at all --
both good and bad.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:06.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One thing you were talking
about, there´s a --

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:08.495
which I did not realize either.
There´s a Halloween tradition.

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:10.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is sort of --
does this come from the fact

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.832
that the Shakers were very
regimented and organized?

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:14.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think it does.

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:16.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even though the Shakers were
never actually living

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:21.808
in Shaker Heights, somehow that
kind of rule-following nature

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:25.745
sank into the ground, and
has permeated the community now.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:29.349 size:88% position:44%
So in Shaker Heights on
Halloween when it´s time

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:33.887
to trick or treat, the city runs
the sirens at the fire station

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.955 size:88% position:44%
at 6:00 to let you know
that it´s time to start.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:38.625
And then they run the sirens
again at 8:00 to tell you that

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
it´s time to stop
trick or treating.

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:42.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought
that everybody did that.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:47.433
-And we didn´t realize
that wasn´t true until --

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
A good girlfriend of mine
who grew up in Shaker Heights

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:51.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
lived near me and
we both have little kids.

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:54.474
And we were talking to our
husbands who didn´t grow up

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:56.843
in Shaker Heights, and so we
said, "Okay, so when do we --

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
When does trick
or treating start?"

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
And our husbands looked at us
and said, "What do mean,

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:02.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
when does it start?
It starts when you

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:04.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
put on the costume
and you go outside

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.085
and you ring a doorbell."

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we said,
"Well, when does it end?

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:10.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, when do you stop?"
And they said,

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What do you mean,
when does it end?

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:15.094
It ends when you come home
and stop ringing doorbells."

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my girlfriend
just looked at me and said,

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, this is just chaos."
-Yeah.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:20.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And now I just have to ask,
is there --

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:24.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
For the rest of your life,
your adult life,

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:28.274
when you hear a fire engine,
do you have a Pavlovian candy?

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A little bit.
-Yeah.

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:30.777 size:78% position:39%
I want to go and ring
somebody´s doorbell.

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:32.512
-To the other guy, "I hope
your house isn´t on fire.

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:34.013
Also, can I have a Kit Kat?"

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:35.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:38.484
You were actually --
So you´ve been doing readings --

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:39.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
Doing a book tour.
And you were --

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:42.121
You rescheduled, thank you
so much for rescheduling

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be here, but you were going
to read

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Shaker Heights tonight.
-I was.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.493
I was supposed to read in my
hometown where the book is set.

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:48.595
So I hope that they forgive me.

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:49.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hope this was
a good enough reason.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:51.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
I think they will forgive you.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:52.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you also --
You know, you talk about

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:55.201 size:88% position:44%
the people in this town.
Do you have any worries

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:58.104
about that versus any other
reading across the country

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you do?
-A little bit, yeah.

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:02.242
I´m kind of nervous about that,
just because it´s --

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:04.544
It´s a little bit writing --
like writing about a relative

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:05.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
or like writing
about your grandma.

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:08.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, you love them
and you want everybody to see

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
the good things about them,
but you also know all

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
their weird habits
and their weird quirks

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:13.786 size:78% position:39%
and you want to kind
of reveal those, too.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.655
-Do you think it´s a good --
If I´m in a Shaker Heights

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
book club, is this
a good book for us?

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:19.592
-I think so.
I think that the Shaker Heights

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.861
population will have a lot
of things to talk about.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.997
I hope they see themselves
in the book, and they also

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:27.300
sort of question, like, "Okay
well, do we mean to do that

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
or is that just
kind of how we do things?"

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And if there´s a character
that they don´t like,

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
I bet they´ll see someone else
in the book club

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:33.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
as that character.
-Yeah.

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:34.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don´t think
they´ll see it´s them.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It´s my next door neighbor.

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:38.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
That´s definitely Megan.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:42.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your parents were scientists.
Your dad worked at NASA?

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:46.052
-He was a physicist.
-And what did they feel when --

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:47.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
That you have two scientists,
when say you want to be

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:48.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
a writer?
-I think they were

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
really nervous, but I think
they kind of knew

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:53.159 size:78% position:39%
it was coming because
I was an early reader

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:55.862
and ever since I was a kid
I was the one who was, like,

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:57.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
off in the corner,
drawing little books

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.731 size:81% position:41%
and making up stories.

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.633
And I used to write plays
and I would make my cousins

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:02.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
perform them.

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:05.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I think they were
nervous, because they just --

00:05:05.772 --> 00:05:07.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
This was a world
they didn´t know.

00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:09.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
They didn´t know how
to do anything.

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:12.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so when I told my mother
that I was going to go

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:15.715
and get a Master of Fine Arts
in Creative Writing, she said,

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:19.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Okay."
And then we got off the phone.

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:20.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the next day she sent me
an e-mail where she said,

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:23.523
"Okay, I´ve talked to my friend
who is the chair of

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:25.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
the English Department here
at our university."

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:27.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was the chair of
the Chemistry Department.

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:30.196
And she said, "He assures me
that a Master of Fine Arts

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:31.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
is a real degree.

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:32.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:35.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that it qualifies you
to teach writing..."

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
which she wrote with
a capital "W,"

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:40.006 size:75% position:38%
...and artsy stuff."

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:41.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so she was like,
"Okay, this is --

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:43.910
you know, I think you´ll be able
to, you know, buy food

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.244 size:84% position:42%
and pay for your rent."

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:47.313
-Well, they were right.
They were right on that account.

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:48.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
And thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations on the book.
-Thank you so much.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:52.085 size:81% position:41%
Celeste Ng, everybody!

00:05:52.085 --> 00:05:54.821
Her new book, "Little Fires
Everywhere" is available now.

